# Cursor Rules Management Guide

## Rule Structure Format

Every cursor rule must follow this exact metadata and content structure:

````markdown
---
description: Short description of the rule's purpose
globs: optional/path/pattern/**/*
alwaysApply: false
---
# Rule Title

Main content explaining the rule with markdown formatting.

1. Step-by-step instructions
2. Code examples
3. Guidelines

Example:
```tsx
// ✅ Good: React functional component with TypeScript and Tailwind
const baseClass = 'rounded-full px-7 py-3.5 inline-flex justify-center items-center gap-2 text-neutral bg-primary transition-all'
const defaultVariantClass = ''
const outlineVariantClass = 'border-1.5 bg-transparent border-primary text-primary'

const variants = {
 variant: {
   default: cn(defaultVariantClass, 'hover:bg-primary-40 active:bg-primary'),
   outline: cn(outlineVariantClass, 'hover:bg-primary-10'),
 },
}

const buttonVariants = cva(baseClass, {
 variants,
 defaultVariants: { variant: 'default' },
})

export interface ButtonProps extends React.ButtonHTMLAttributes<HTMLButtonElement>,
 VariantProps<typeof buttonVariants> {
 asChild?: boolean
}

const Button = React.forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(
 ({ className, variant, asChild = false, ...props }, ref) => {
   const Comp = asChild ? Slot : 'button'
   return <Comp className={cn(buttonVariants({ variant, className }))} ref={ref} {...props} />
 }
)

// ❌ Bad: Missing TypeScript interface and using inline styles
export const Button = ({ variant, children, onClick }) => {
  return (
    <button style={{color: 'red'}} onClick={onClick}>
      {children}
    </button>
  )
}
```
````

## File Organization

### Required Location

All cursor rule files **must** be placed in:

<path_to_rules>PROJECT_ROOT/.cursor/rules/</path_to_rules>

### Directory Structure

<directory_structure>
PROJECT_ROOT/
├── .cursor/
│   └── rules/
│       ├── your-rule-name.mdc
│       ├── another-rule.mdc
│       └── cursor-rules.mdc
└── ...
</directory_structure>

### Naming Conventions

- Use **kebab-case** for all rule filenames
- Always use **.mdc** extension
- Make names **descriptive** of the rule's purpose
- Examples suitable for React project:
  - `react-components.mdc` - Component patterns and conventions
  - `tailwind-styling.mdc` - Tailwind CSS 4 styling guidelines
  - `shadcn-components.mdc` - Shadcn component usage and customization
  - `typescript-react.mdc` - TypeScript patterns in React
  - `atomic-design.mdc` - Atomic design structure for components
  - `i18n-implementation.mdc` - Internationalization patterns with react-i18next

## Content Guidelines

### Writing Effective Rules

1. **Be specific and actionable** - Provide clear instructions
2. **Include code examples** - Show both good and bad practices
3. **Reference existing files** - Use `@filename.ext` format
4. **Keep it focused** - One rule per concern/pattern
5. **Add context** - Explain why the rule exists

### Code Examples Format for React + Tailwind CSS 4

```tsx
// ✅ Good: React component with Tailwind CSS 4 and proper TypeScript
interface CardProps {
  title: string
  description?: string
  variant?: 'default' | 'outlined'
  className?: string
}

export const Card: React.FC<CardProps> = ({
  title,
  description,
  variant = 'default',
  className = ''
}) => {
  return (
    <div className={cn(
      'rounded-lg border bg-card text-card-foreground shadow-sm',
      variant === 'outlined' && 'border-2',
      className
    )}>
      <div className="p-6">
        <h3 className="text-2xl font-semibold leading-none tracking-tight">{title}</h3>
        {description && (
          <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-2">{description}</p>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>
  )
}

// ❌ Bad: Inline styles, no TypeScript, unclear structure
export const Card = ({ title, description }) => {
  return (
    <div style={{ border: '1px solid gray', padding: '20px' }} className="color-[#1a1a1a]">
      <h3>{title}</h3>
      <p>{description}</p>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### File References

When referencing project files in rules, use this pattern to mention other files:

```markdown
[file.tsx](/path/to/file.tsx)
```

## Forbidden Locations

**Never** place rule files in:
- Project root directory
- Any subdirectory outside `.cursor/rules/`
- Component directories
- Source code folders
- Documentation folders

