## Best Practices for React Project

### Rule Creation Checklist
- [ ] File placed in `.cursor/rules/` directory
- [ ] Filename uses kebab-case with `.mdc` extension
- [ ] Includes proper metadata section
- [ ] Contains clear title and sections
- [ ] Provides both good and bad examples with React/TypeScript
- [ ] References relevant project files (main.css, components, utils.ts, etc.)
- [ ] Follows consistent formatting
- [ ] Uses Tailwind CSS classes instead of inline styles in examples
- [ ] Includes TypeScript interfaces and proper typing
- [ ] Compatible with Shadcn component patterns

### React-Specific Guidelines
- **Component Examples**: Always use functional components with hooks
- **TypeScript Typing**: Define interfaces for all props
- **Tailwind Usage**: Prefer utility classes, avoid custom CSS
- **Shadcn Integration**: Use `cn()` helper for conditional styling
- **Atomic Design**: Follow atoms/molecules/organisms structure
- **i18n Support**: Include internationalization in examples when relevant

### Maintenance for React Codebase
- **Review regularly** - Keep rules updated with React/Tailwind changes
- **Update examples** - Ensure code samples reflect current component patterns
- **Cross-reference** - Link related rules (React + Tailwind + Shadcn)
- **Document changes** - Update rules when component patterns evolve
- **Monitor dependencies** - Update when Tailwind CSS 4 or Shadcn has updates
- **Test compatibility** - Ensure examples work with current project setup
